---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Legal', url: '/legal/' },
  { name: 'Disclaimer', url: '/legal/disclaimer/' },
];
const schemas = [buildBreadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs)];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer: Calculators Are for Information Only"
  description="Calctube calculators provide general information and educational estimates. They are not financial, medical, tax, legal, or investment advice."
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <section class="container-prose pt-10 pb-16 md:pt-14 md:pb-24">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6">
      <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        {breadcrumbs.map((item, idx) => (
          <li class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
            {idx === breadcrumbs.length - 1 ? (
              <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-ink-900 text-white font-bold border-2 border-ink-900">{item.name}</span>
            ) : (
              <>
                <a href={item.url} class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-white border-2 border-ink-200 text-ink-700 font-semibold hover:border-ink-900 hover:text-ink-900 no-underline transition-colors">{item.name}</a>
                <svg class="w-3 h-3 text-ink-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
              </>
            )}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <span class="chip-yellow mb-4">⚠️ Disclaimer</span>
    <h1 class="!text-4xl sm:!text-5xl !font-extrabold !tracking-tight !leading-[1.05] text-ink-900 mt-4" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.035em;">
      Calculators are for information only.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink-700 font-medium leading-relaxed">
      Every calculator on Calctube is built to help you work something out quickly. It is not a
      substitute for advice from a qualified professional who knows your situation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">Not professional advice</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      The results, estimates, and reference figures produced by Calctube calculators are general
      information and educational content. They do not constitute financial, investment, lending,
      accounting, tax, legal, medical, health, fitness, or other professional advice, and they should
      not be relied upon as such. Nothing on this site creates a professional-client relationship
      between you and Calctube.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">Verify before you act</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      Calculator outputs depend entirely on the inputs you supply and on the assumptions built into the
      formula. A realistic answer still depends on things a calculator cannot see: your full financial
      position, the fees and charges your lender actually charges, the specific product terms you are
      signing for, your medical history, or the tax treatment that applies to you personally.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      Before you commit money, sign a contract, change a mortgage, start an investment plan, or make a
      health decision, take the figure from the calculator and check it against the actual terms from
      your lender, provider, accountant, tax adviser, doctor, or other licensed professional. Where
      the two disagree, the provider's current written terms and a qualified professional's advice
      are the ones that count.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">Rates, prices, and reference data</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      Interest rates, exchange rates, tax brackets, price indices, inflation assumptions, and other
      reference data used by Calctube are drawn from public sources and are provided as indicative
      ranges. They change frequently, may be delayed or incomplete, and may not reflect what you are
      offered. Calctube is not responsible for the accuracy, timeliness, or fitness of any reference
      figure for your particular use.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">Health calculators in particular</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      The health calculators on this site — including body mass index, basal metabolic rate, total
      daily energy expenditure, calorie, and body fat estimates — are general screening tools based
      on population-level formulas. They are not diagnostic devices. They do not account for your
      medical history, medications, conditions, age-specific guidance, or the many factors that a
      clinician would consider. Do not use them to diagnose, treat, cure, or manage any condition,
      and do not change your diet, exercise, or medication on the basis of their output. Speak to a
      qualified healthcare professional about your individual circumstances, especially if you are
      pregnant, managing a chronic condition, injured, or making changes to prescribed treatment.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      If you have a medical emergency, contact your local emergency number or a qualified healthcare
      provider immediately. Do not rely on this website or anything on it for urgent medical needs.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      Calctube and its calculators are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, without
      warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any implied warranties of merchantability,
      fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement. To the maximum extent permitted
      by law, Calctube and its operators are not liable for any loss or damage, including lost profits,
      lost savings, lost data, or indirect or consequential loss, arising from your use of, or
      reliance on, anything on this site. You accept full responsibility for how you use the results.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-2xl sm:!text-3xl !font-extrabold text-ink-900 !mt-10" style="font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;">Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
      We take accuracy seriously and fix errors as we find them. If a calculator produces a result you
      believe is wrong, tell us: email <a href="mailto:bugs@calctube.com" class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2">bugs@calctube.com</a>
      with the page, the inputs you used, and the result you expected. If a figure on this site is
      misleading in a way that could affect a decision, please report it and we will review it.
    </p>

    <div class="card mt-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
        This disclaimer supplements, and does not replace, our
        <a href="/legal/terms/" class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2">Terms of Service</a>
        and <a href="/legal/privacy/" class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2">Privacy Policy</a>.
        It applies to every page and every calculator on Calctube.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
